---
title: "How do the two notebook section surfaces differ?"
accTitle: "Glued hash versus bullet-start hash"
accDescr: "Glued at-nb hash keeps a selector on one item or list. Bullet-start hash rewrites to an ALL-CAPS grouping header whose nested notes become that H2."
config:
  flowchart:
    rankSpacing: 16
    nodeSpacing: 18
    wrappingWidth: 200
---
flowchart TD
  G1["`**Glued: @nb#git note**<br/>one note in Git`"]
  G2["`**Glued: @nb#git list**<br/>every bullet in Git`"]
  B1["`**Bullet: - #git**<br/>rewrites to GIT`"]
  B2["`**Bullet nested notes**<br/>become that H2`"]
  RESOLVE["`**Shared resolver**<br/>exact title or whole slug`"]
  WRITE["`**## Git**<br/>create on demand`"]
  G1 --> RESOLVE
  G2 --> RESOLVE
  B1 -.->|"opens nested dash"| B2
  B2 -.-> RESOLVE
  RESOLVE ==> WRITE
  classDef focus fill:#E8F1FB,stroke:#3B78C2,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#0F2E52
  classDef outcome fill:#E7F5EC,stroke:#2E7D4F,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#123D24
  classDef muted fill:#F3F4F6,stroke:#6B7280,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#1F2937
  classDef proposed stroke-dasharray:5 3
  class G1,G2,B1,B2 focus
  class B1,B2 proposed
  class WRITE outcome
  class RESOLVE muted
